/g><g id=\"patch_4\"><path d=\"M 168.75013 139.04 L 258.60987 139.04 L 258.60987 54.404397 L 168.75013 54.404397 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p0a245dd4e9)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_5\"><path d=\"M 281.074805 139.04 L 370.934545 139.04 L 370.934545 17.6 L 281.074805 17.6 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p0a245dd4e9)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_6\"><path d=\"M 40.7 139.04 L 40.7 11.528 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_7\"><path d=\"M 40.7 139.04 L 386.66 139.04 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_10\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(96.555325 62.626667) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_11\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(208.88 52.204397) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\" d=\"M 1184 2573 L 1670 2573 Q 2125 2573 2352 2784 Q 2579 2995 2579 3315 L 2579 3360 Q 2579 3712 2358 3888 Q 2138 4064 1779 4064 Q 1434 4064 1216 3913 Q 998 3763 858 3507 L 461 3814 Q 576 3994 749 4160 Q 922 4326 1178 4435 Q 1434 4544 1792 4544 Q 2170 4544 2477 4413 Q 2784 4282 2966 4032 Q 3149 3782 3149 3418 Q 3149 2989 2899 2726 Q 2650 2464 2291 2374 L 2291 2349 Q 2534 2304 2748 2166 Q 2963 2029 3097 1795 Q 3232 1562 3232 1222 Q 3232 838 3043 547 Q 2854 256 2512 89 Q 2170 -77 1715 -77 Q 1331 -77 1059 35 Q 787 147 598 320 Q 410 493 269 685 L 672 992 Q 845 730 1072 566 Q 1299 403 1709 403 Q 2182 403 2425 620 Q 2669 838 2669 1229 L 2669 1280 Q 2669 1677 2425 1891 Q 2182 2106 1709 2106 L 1184 2106 L 1184 2573 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_12\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(321.204675 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-43\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p0a245dd4e9\"><rect x=\"40.7\" y=\"11.528\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Customers per day","note":null},"answer":"<p>Profit = customers × $24 × 310 days × 45% − $210k.</p> <ul><li>Landlord, 90 a day: <b>$91k</b>, payback 1.8 years</li> <li>Benchmark, 55 a day: <b>−$26k</b>: a loss</li></ul> <p>Break-even: $210k ÷ ($24 × 310 × 45%) = <b>62.7 customers a day</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> the decision depends entirely on whose forecast is right. On Fillhaus's own experience, the shop would lose money.</p>"},{"q":"At 55 customers a day, what basket size would Fillhaus need to break even? How could it get there?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Basket needed: $210k ÷ (55 × 310 × 45%) = <b>$27.37</b>, 14% more than today.</p> <ul><li>Bundles of everyday staples (rice, oats, detergent) sold by the kilo</li><li>Click-and-collect refills prepared in advance (also saves staff time)</li> <li>Workplace orders: offices refilling cleaning products monthly</li><li>Higher-margin own-brand products</li></ul>"},{"q":"How would you negotiate with the landlord?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Turnover-based or stepped rent</b> for the first two years, so the landlord shares the footfall risk</li> <li><b>Fit-out contribution</b>, common for anchor-style tenants in a new development</li> <li><b>Break clause</b> after 24 months if footfall targets aren't met</li> <li>Ask for <b>footfall data</b> from the landlord's other centres to back up the 90 a day</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Don't sign on the current terms. The shop works only if the landlord's 90 customers a day is right ($91k profit); at the 55 a day Fillhaus's own shops achieve, it loses about $26k a year, with break-even at 63 customers. I recommend negotiating turnover-based rent and a fit-out contribution so the landlord shares the risk, and raising the basket towards $27 through bundles and workplace orders. Risk: a new development can take years to fill. Next step: request the landlord's footfall data from comparable centres.","great":["Questions the source of the forecast","Uses the client's own shops as a benchmark","Finds break-even in customers and in basket size","Turns the analysis into a negotiation"],"id":33,"slug":"fillhaus-refill"}